tities into:\n  - `nodeMap: Map<Long, MiniNode>` — all nodes with lat/lon + tags\n  - `allWays: List<Way>` — all ways (for later classification)\n  - `relationWays: Map<Long, List<MiniMember>>` — multipolygon/boundary relations\n\n#### b) Data organization (lines 155–220)\n\nThe data is split into **three layers**:\n1. **Point Layer** — nodes that have tags AND are NOT referenced by any way (e.g., standalone shops, bus stops, places)\n2. **Line Layer** — non-closed ways (roads, rivers, railways)\n3. **Polygon Layer** — closed ways (buildings, landuse areas) + ways referenced by multipolygon relations\n\n#### c) GIS model classes used (from `dsol-animation-gis-4.2.2.jar`)\n\n```\nGisMap\n  ├── name: String\n  └── layers: List<Layer>\n\nLayer\n  ├── name: String\n  ├── display: boolean\n  ├── transform: boolean\n  └── features: List<FeatureInterface>  (actually Feature)\n\nFeature (implements FeatureInterface)\n  ├── key: String         (e.g. \"highway\", \"building\")\n  ├── value: String       (e.g. \"residential\", \"yes\")\n  ├── fillColor: Color\n  ├── outlineColor: Color\n  └── shapes: List<GisObject>\n\nGisObject\n  ├── path: SerializablePath   (polyline/polygon geometry)\n  └── attributeValues: String[]  ([osmId, mainKey, tagSummary, nodeCount])\n```\n\n#### d) Feature classification (line 295)\n\nEach OSM element is categorized by a priority-based main tag key:\n```\nhighway > building > waterway > landuse > natural > railway > amenity > leisure > boundary > power > barrier > place > first tag key\n```\n\n#### e) Color scheme (line 334)\n\nEach feature category gets a fixed color via a switch expression.\n\n#### f) Output (lines 450–481)\n\nThe `main()` method parses `src/main/resources/jiangxi-260526.osm.pbf`, then prints:\n- Total counts (Nodes, Ways, Relations)\n- Per-layer statistics (feature type breakdown)\n- Sample geometries (first 8 per layer)\n\n### 5. Test Files Related to OSM Parsing\n\n**There are zero test files.** The `src/test/java/` directory